From 8ad1ab7eb5af3a96f754310d76760886bc7fc70b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tillmann Severin <tillmann.severin@mailbox.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 19:55:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 26/26] media: rc: ir-hix5hd2: report a real duration for the
 trailing space

When a received symbol is wider than IR_CFG_SYMBOL_MAXWIDTH the driver
marks the receiver idle via ir_raw_event_set_idle(). That helper submits
dev->raw->this_ev, but this_ev is only ever populated by
ir_raw_event_store_edge() and ir_raw_event_store_with_filter(), neither
of which this driver uses. The event therefore always carries a zero
duration, which makes rc-core complain

  rc rc0: nonsensical timing event of duration 0

and, more importantly, breaks decoding of trailing spaces. An NEC repeat
frame ends on such a symbol, so its trailer space arrives as 0us and
fails the decoder's geq_margin() check, meaning a held-down key never
repeats.

Store an explicit timeout event using the receiver timeout instead. The
idle flag itself is not used by this driver, as it only calls
ir_raw_event_store() and never leaves idle mode again.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/rc/ir-hix5hd2.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/rc/ir-hix5hd2.c b/drivers/media/rc/ir-hix5hd2.c
index bb0f95833df5..916d3ee5bc42 100644
--- a/drivers/media/rc/ir-hix5hd2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/rc/ir-hix5hd2.c
@@ -225,7 +225,10 @@ static irqreturn_t hix5hd2_ir_rx_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 				ev.pulse = false;
 				ir_raw_event_store(priv->rdev, &ev);
 			} else {
-				ir_raw_event_set_idle(priv->rdev, true);
+				ev.duration = priv->rdev->timeout;
+				ev.pulse = false;
+				ev.timeout = true;
+				ir_raw_event_store(priv->rdev, &ev);
 			}
 		}
 
